\title{Subtyping}
\date{2026-06-11T21:14:46Z}
\import{swarm-macros}

\p{We have a mild form of subtyping, in that we can always weaken a judgment by adding more capabilities:

\rules{
  \inferrule
    {\swty{\Gamma}{t}{\tau}{\Delta} \\ \Delta \subseteq \Delta'}
    {\swty{\Gamma}{t}{\tau}{\Delta'}}
}

So the judgment \swty{\Gamma}{t}{\tau}{\Delta} does not claim that the capabilities #{\Delta} are \em{necessary} (though in practice, of course, we often want to try to compute a minimal #{\Delta} that will work).  It merely claims that #{\Delta} are \em{sufficient}: any robot with all the capabilities in #{\Delta} is guaranteed to be able to evaluate #{t}.

}
